### Findings

#### 1. [`ReadyGate`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L7-L29) & `native-ready` in [`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L170-L204)

* **Lost Wakeups (Resolved):** In [`NativeSender::send`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L191-L203), the message is published to `self.tx` before [`ReadyGate::notify`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L13-L18) acquires `self.0`. On the worker side ([`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L434-L442)), [`ReadyGate::finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L22-L28) holds that same gate mutex while polling lookahead (`mailbox.rx.try_recv()` into `mailbox.buffered`).
  * If [`notify`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L13-L18) wins the gate lock while a worker is active, `*scheduled` is already `true` and the subsequent [`finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L22-L28) is guaranteed to observe the already-sent item via `try_recv()`.
  * If [`finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L22-L28) wins the gate lock and sees an empty channel, it sets `*scheduled = false` before releasing the lock, so the waiting [`notify`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L13-L18) observes `*scheduled == false`, transitions it to `true`, and enqueues the actor. No wakeup can be lost.
* **Duplicates & Ownership (Resolved):** A ready token (`Some(id)`) is emitted only when `*scheduled` transitions `false -> true` in [`notify`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L13-L18) or remains `true` on non-empty lookahead in [`finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L22-L28). At most one runnable token per actor exists in the ready queue. Even if a newly scheduled token is popped by a second worker before the first worker finishes updating `mailbox.batch_hint` ([`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L443-L451)), the first worker holds `actor.mailbox` across the entire turn including [`finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L414-L451), serializing access to [`ReadyMailbox`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L175-L179) (`rx`, `buffered`, and `batch_hint`).
* **Lock Ordering & Deadlock Freedom (Resolved):**
  * Workers acquire and immediately release `ready_rxs` ([`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L411)), then lock `actor.mailbox` ([`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L414)), and inside [`finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs#L22-L28) lock `gate.0` and `tx.send`.
  * Producers complete `self.tx.send(probe)` before acquiring `gate.0` and calling `signal.ready.send`, and never lock `actor.mailbox` or `ready_rxs`.
  * Lock acquisition forms a strict DAG (`actor.mailbox` $\rightarrow$ `gate.0` $\rightarrow$ ready channel). Blocking on a full bounded mailbox (`mpsc::sync_channel`) occurs before `gate.0` is taken, so workers can always drain the mailbox.
* **Shutdown (Clean for Benchmark Lifecycle):** Shutdown ([`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L798-L806)) runs only after all warmup and measured replies have been collected. Sending `None` once per `worker` across `txs[worker % txs.len()]` delivers one termination sentinel per worker in both `global` (`groups == 1`, shared `Arc<Mutex<Receiver>>`) and `local` (`groups == config.workers`, one queue per worker) scheduler modes.

#### 2. [`ready_gate_loom.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/ready_gate_loom.rs#L1-L45)

* [`publish_racing_finish_retains_exactly_one_ready_token`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/ready_gate_loom.rs#L6-L44) directly imports [`support/ready_gate.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/ready_gate.rs) and verifies the single-token and no-lost-wakeup invariants under 2-producer / 1-worker races.
* **Minor Modeling Difference (Non-blocker):** The test protects the mock mailbox `messages` with a single `loom::sync::Mutex` held by the worker from pop through [`g.finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/tests/ready_gate_loom.rs#L24-L27). In [`designs.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L192-L199), producer `mpsc::SyncSender::send` can interleave between the worker's batch loop and [`actor.gate.finish`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/designs.rs#L434-L442) while `actor.mailbox` is held. Because the test also runs producers before the worker acquires `m` in other schedules, the critical `notify` vs. `finish` gate interleavings are still exercised.

#### 3. [`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L1-L172)

* **Cross-Thread Wakeup & Timing Window (Resolved):** Enabling `monoio`'s `sync` feature in [`Cargo.toml`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/Cargo.toml#L10) activates thread-safe cross-thread waker support on Monoio's drivers, so firing the `futures::channel::oneshot` start gates from the main thread ([`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L147-L149)) reliably wakes tasks parked on `gate.await` ([`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L104)). Recording `finished.send(Instant::now())` inside the runtime block ([`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L86), [`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs#L125)) captures completion prior to runtime drop and socket teardown.

#### 4. Remaining Blockers vs. Disclosed Prototype Semantics

* **Real Remaining Blockers:** None for the benchmark and experiment scope.
* **Already-Disclosed Prototype Limitations (Not Blockers):** As documented in [`EXPERIMENTS.md`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/benchmarks/EXPERIMENTS.md#L26-L36), `native-ready` omits full actor lifecycle features (cancellation, panic isolation, timers, dynamic actor registration, async suspension, and cyclic bounded-send deadlock avoidance), `local-ready` uses static modulo placement without work stealing, and [`io_mux.rs`](file:///private/tmp/spawned-scenario-tests/concurrency/benches/support/io_mux.rs) pairs a single-thread multiplexed client against a thread-per-connection blocking echo server and does not bridge Monoio's `!Send` futures to `Send` actor handlers.
